Z||000000||Bill 88||08-13-99||05:30 PM||||I am new at this so please bear with me.  I have a 88 SC with 4cyl and 5 speed and a 86 sc with V6 and 4 speed.  I want to to put the V6 into the 88.  What kind of problems am I looking forward to?  Any help would be appreciated.  Thanks  
Z||000001||PaUL||08-13-99||06:03 PM||||SCCAfiero is the guy to talk to. He did this exact same swap a few weeks ago.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-13-99||06:36 PM||||First off you will need a new front engine mount for an 88 V6 Fiero or extend the foot on the original mount about 2 inches. You will also need to drill the 88 cradle to mount the motor strut. (Looks like a tiny shock) The 88's didn't not use this. If you don't do these two things your motor will sit crooked.<p>If you have the complete donor car things will go smooth. First thing I did was install the 86 interior in my 88. The 4 cylinder gauge pod will not interchange with the V6 gauges in any way. Then while the dash was out I installed the V6 wiring harness. The harness is hard to wiggle into place but it is possible. MAKE SURE TO PUT IN THE V6 THROTTLE CABLE WHILE YOU HAVE IT RIPPED APART. <p>If you have any questions just post them here for everyone's enjoyment <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><br>
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-14-99||01:28 AM||||To see most of my progress see "HELP please"
